.\" Man page for blitzctl
.\" Generated from source; do not edit manually.
.\"
.TH BLITZCTL 1 "2026-09-08" "0.12.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blitzctl \- control utility for the apt-blitz on-disk cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blitzctl
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,COMMAND\/\fR [\fI\,ARGS\/\fR]
.br
.B blitzctl cache
\fI\,SUBCOMMAND\/\fR [\fI\,ARGS\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBblitzctl\fR is a companion utility for the \fBapt-blitz\fR HTTP forward
proxy.  It inspects and manages the on-disk cache directly against the
SQLite database, so it can be used while the proxy is running.
.P
The cache directory is resolved the same way as the service: the YAML
\fIcache_dir\fR option, then the \fBPROXY_CACHE_DIR\fR environment variable,
then the compiled-in default \fB/var/cache/apt-blitz\fR.  The
.B \-\-cache\-dir
option overrides it.
.P
Every command accepts a \fIHOST\fR argument that may be a configured
.B \-\-url\-map
alias or the real upstream host.  Filtering matches either form, and output
is shown in the matching alias/real perspective.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-dir \fI\,PATH\/\fR
Cache directory (overrides config/env default).
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print help information and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH CACHE SUBCOMMANDS
.SS hosts
List cached resource hosts with totals (alias, real host, size, file count).
.br
Usage: \fBblitzctl cache hosts\fR
.SS tree
Show the per-host resource filesystem tree.  Individual files are hidden by
default; use \fB\-\-files\fR/\fB\-f\fR to list them.
.br
Usage: \fBblitzctl cache tree\fR \fIHOST\fR [\fIPATH\fR]
.br
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-files
Also list individual cached files.
.SS find
Search files and folders within a host by name.  \fB*\fR matches any run of
characters and \fB?\fR matches any single character; the match is
case-insensitive.  A \fB/\fR in the query matches against the full path,
otherwise the match is against the name (last component).
.br
Usage: \fBblitzctl cache find\fR \fIHOST\fR \fIQUERY\fR
.SS ls
List cached entries like the system \fB\&ls\fR over the cache URL namespace,
optionally limited to \fIHOST\fR and a \fIPATH\fR prefix or glob.  Both take
the form \fBblitzctl cache ls\fR [\fIHOST\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]; when \fIHOST\fR
is omitted all cached hosts are listed.  \fIHOST\fR and \fIPATH\fR are
separate positional arguments: URLs and single\-token \fBhost/path\fR
selectors are rejected.
.br
Usage: \fBblitzctl cache ls\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIHOST\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-long
Long format: cached date, last access, seconds until expiry, size.
.TP
.B \-\-human
Human-readable sizes (e.g. \fB1.0 MiB\fR).
.TP
.B \-R, \-\-recursive
Recurse into subdirectories.
.TP
.B \-1, \-\-oneline
Print one entry per line (default when output is not a terminal).
.TP
.B \-N, \-\-name
Sort by name (default).
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-time
Sort by last access time (newest first).
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-cached
Sort by cache time (\fIcached_at\fR, newest first).
.TP
.B \-S, \-\-size
Sort by size (largest first).
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-reverse
Reverse the sort order.
.P
Directories are always listed first, regardless of the sort key.
.SS info
Show details of a single cached file: URL, host/path in the active
perspective, size, cached time, last access, freshness (seconds until
expiry), content type, and the stored file location.
.br
Usage: \fBblitzctl cache info\fR \fIHOST\fR \fIPATH\fR
.SS rm
Remove cached entries: all entries, or only those matching \fITARGET\fR
(\fBhost\fR or \fBhost/path\fR, prefix or exact file).  Removing the entire
cache asks for confirmation (type \fByes\fR) unless \fB\-\-yes\fR is given.
.br
Usage: \fBblitzctl cache rm\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITARGET\fR]
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt (full removal only).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List cached hosts:
.RS
.B blitzctl cache hosts
.RE
.TP
Browse a host's filesystem tree including files:
.RS
.B blitzctl cache tree
\fIdeb.debian.org\fR
.B \-\-files
.RE
.TP
Search for \fI.deb\fR packages on a host:
.RS
.B blitzctl cache find
\fIdeb.debian.org\fR
.B "*\.deb"
.RE
.TP
List the largest cached entries under a path:
.RS
.B blitzctl cache ls
.B \-S
\fIsecurity.debian.org\fR
\fIpool\fR
.RE
.TP
Show details of a single cached file:
.RS
.B blitzctl cache info
\fIdeb.debian.org\fR
\fIpool/main/a/apt_1.0_all.deb\fR
.RE
.TP
Remove cached entries for a host selector:
.RS
.B blitzctl cache rm
\fIdeb.debian.org\fR
.B \-\-yes
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/cache/apt-blitz
Default cache directory (contains the \fBcache.db\fR SQLite database and the
sharded cached files).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-blitz (1)